-- Differential-parity probe for the EITHER builtin (LEFT / RIGHT) under
-- CONSIDER — the ledger #10 fix. EITHER a b is a payload-CARRYING ADT
-- from the prelude (like MAYBE), not a nullary enum, so the CONSIDER
-- lowering used to refuse the RIGHT/LEFT constructor patterns
-- ("could not be resolved to an enum tag by the WASM backend").
--
-- Every exported function CONSTRUCTS the EITHER internally (so no EITHER
-- value crosses the ABI boundary) and takes only scalar inputs, then
-- dispatches on RIGHT vs LEFT and USES the bound payload. The cases
-- deliberately separate:
--   * which branch is taken (LEFT vs RIGHT — tag resolution), and
--   * the payload value from the tag (1.0 / 0.0) and from the other
--     branch's value (payload binding).
-- A broken tag test or a slot-0-vs-slot-1 payload bug therefore diverges
-- from jl4-service. These mirror orchestrator.l4's isViolation /
-- getConfidence / extractText shapes with the IO (JSONDECODE / POST)
-- removed.

IMPORT prelude

-- Build RIGHT for positive n, LEFT for non-positive. RIGHT carries the
-- NUMBER itself (distinct from the tag 1.0); LEFT carries a STRING.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING NUMBER
`classify number` MEANS
  IF n GREATER THAN 0
  THEN RIGHT n
  ELSE LEFT "non-positive"

-- RIGHT branch doubles the bound payload; LEFT branch returns the
-- negated length of the bound message. Tag swap ⇒ payload type mismatch;
-- slot-0 payload bug ⇒ RIGHT yields 2 (tag*2) instead of n*2.
@export Dispatch on EITHER: RIGHT doubles payload, LEFT gives -length
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`either dispatch` MEANS
  CONSIDER `classify number` n
    WHEN RIGHT v THEN v TIMES 2
    WHEN LEFT  s THEN 0 MINUS STRINGLENGTH s

-- Mirrors getConfidence: RIGHT payload used directly, LEFT ⇒ sentinel 0.
@export Confidence from EITHER (RIGHT payload, else 0)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`either confidence` MEANS
  CONSIDER `classify number` n
    WHEN RIGHT v THEN v
    WHEN LEFT  s THEN 0

-- Mirrors isViolation: RIGHT carries a BOOLEAN payload, LEFT ⇒ FALSE.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING BOOLEAN
`classify verdict` MEANS
  IF n GREATER THAN 10
  THEN RIGHT TRUE
  ELSE IF n GREATER THAN 0
       THEN RIGHT FALSE
       ELSE LEFT "no verdict"

@export Verdict from EITHER (RIGHT boolean payload, else FALSE)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`either verdict` MEANS
  CONSIDER `classify verdict` n
    WHEN RIGHT b THEN b
    WHEN LEFT  s THEN FALSE

-- Mirrors extractText: RIGHT carries a LIST, and the RIGHT branch runs a
-- NESTED CONSIDER over that list (FOLLOWED BY / EMPTY); LEFT ⇒ negated
-- message length. Exercises payload binding of a compound (list) payload
-- plus a nested CONSIDER inside the RIGHT arm.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING (LIST OF NUMBER)
`classify list` MEANS
  IF n GREATER THAN 0
  THEN RIGHT (LIST n, n PLUS 1, n PLUS 2)
  ELSE LEFT "empty"

@export Nested CONSIDER over EITHER-of-LIST (head, else -length)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`either nested` MEANS
  CONSIDER `classify list` n
    WHEN RIGHT xs THEN
      CONSIDER xs
        WHEN h FOLLOWED BY rest THEN h
        WHEN EMPTY THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN LEFT s THEN 0 MINUS STRINGLENGTH s
